WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.020
From The Garden of Eden to the top corner
of your English teacher’s desk, apples have

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:11.059
played an equal role in history’s most remarkable
days and also its most mundane.

00:00:11.059 --> 00:00:15.639
The sounds of teeth snapping through the skin,
sinking into flesh, and spitting out seeds

00:00:15.639 --> 00:00:18.430
echo through space forever and onward.

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:22.730
And for most of our earthly hours consumed
by appetite, it has been documented to be

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:27.750
a lopsided relationship between these two
things, man and apple.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:32.960
Man getting the sweet taste and abundant nutrients,
apples getting nothing but pain and stomach

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.000
acids.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.079
But this story is found not in our history.

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:42.149
Buried in the lawful patterns of predator
and prey, we stumble upon an irregularity,

00:00:42.149 --> 00:00:47.129
an inversion, an instance of apples biting
back.

00:00:47.129 --> 00:00:54.920
SCP-4608, also known as APPLESEED, was a 60-acre
apple orchard containing over 22,000 trees,

00:00:54.920 --> 00:01:00.590
located just on the outskirts of Milan, Indiana
– a town so small it strains your eyes as

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:04.400
you squint to find it with a microscope hovering
just over a map.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:10.070
And to see what was actually happening within
the curious fringes of society took even greater

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:14.340
exploration, not just of the eyes but also
of the mind.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:19.290
Because what would eventually be seen would
not so easily be comprehended.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:23.770
Physical senses are just the surface, and
we need to go deeper.

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:28.590
Our story begins with a logging company looking
to take ownership of the most fertile land

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:33.420
they could find in the Great Lake Region,
ideally land that overproduces conifer growth

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:37.579
so that the return on their investment would
be plentiful and perpetual.

00:01:37.579 --> 00:01:40.170
These lumberjacked men knew what they wanted.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:44.630
Beneath their red flannel shirts and muddy
boots was a deep intelligence and understanding

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:45.719
of nature.

00:01:45.719 --> 00:01:49.860
Their process of assessing the land’s value
was meticulously calculated.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:54.229
They knew the soil, both by the experience
of their callused hands and the literature

00:01:54.229 --> 00:01:55.229
of their study.

00:01:55.229 --> 00:01:59.310
They tracked various bird species’ migration
patterns in the area to assess what kind of

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:03.509
seeds they’d be carrying and contributing
to soil by way of their stool.

00:02:03.509 --> 00:02:08.180
They understood the local laws relating to
clear cutting and conservation and how both

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:10.380
would affect their profit margins.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:13.970
This is all to say, it wasn’t just a speculative
purchase.

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:17.300
This was planned, thought through, and dwelled
on.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:23.740
And yet, even then, with scrupulous eyes and
a careful crew, they missed the warning signs.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:26.980
SCP-4608 checked all their boxes…and then
some.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.860
What could go wrong?

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:34.070
And so they acquired the land, unwittingly
purchasing the peril that came with it.

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:38.450
On the first day of owning the property, one
crew member noticed the branches did not sway

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:40.610
in the same direction as the wind blew.

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:45.000
He noticed the leaves didn’t float down
in agreement with their feathery weight, but

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:49.760
rather crashed to the soil like two-dimensional
anvils and grand pianos.

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:54.530
The roots were not ones you simply trip over,
instead, it seemed as if they stuck their

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:56.370
leg out to trip you.

00:02:56.370 --> 00:03:00.890
When birds perched themselves up high and
sang their songs, their cadence carried all

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:03.040
the eeriness of an SOS.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:07.090
With all of this said, he was happy to have
acquired the land, and having already picked

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:12.319
up and moved his family from the West Coast
to now live and work out in Milan, Indiana,

00:03:12.319 --> 00:03:15.850
he decided it best to look past his concerns.

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:19.980
After all, it was the first day on the new
site, and excitement was in the air…but

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:24.180
with it also an amorphous, anxious energy.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:29.790
During the first logging expedition within
SCP-4608, this same member of the crew hiked

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:33.880
the grounds to better familiarize himself
with the environment he’d be working on,

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:38.340
hopeful that if he managed the land properly
and extracted the lumber as efficiently as

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:42.900
his late father did, he would be able to help
build the business and give his children the

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.810
life he always promised them.

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:48.840
He brought with him his notepad and took detailed
records of his surroundings.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:53.660
He figured to achieve his goals and sustain
long-term yields, he’d have to cooperate

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:54.900
with his environment.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:58.870
But he never questioned if his environment
wanted to cooperate with him.

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:01.520
Would this question have changed the course
of action?

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:06.370
Or is brooding on the preference of plants
an empty gesture, best left for hippies at

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:07.370
Woodstock?

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:12.200
Either way, the orchard let it be known how
it felt about a collaboration when hours later

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.050
the man was found dead.

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:18.700
It was first believed by his coworkers to
be a result of a safety equipment malfunction.

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:22.840
Maybe it was a simple matter of thinking the
skidder was in park when really it was in

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:23.840
neutral.

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:27.310
Maybe the Knuckle-boom Loader went on the
fritz how it does when the humidity ramps

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:28.310
up.

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:33.310
Maybe machinery really was to blame, in which
case you call it a fluke and ask no more.

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:36.960
After all, there’s only so many questions
you can ask a robot.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:41.070
But initial belief is a fickle thing… and
it wasn’t long until first impressions were

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:44.010
called into question by the courts of critical
thinking.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:46.970
The questions of the crew, however, only rang
briefly.

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:49.690
Because shortly after the first death fell
a sequence of others.

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:54.260
In a matter of days, all of the remaining
crew members were declared dead or missing,

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:59.620
a word reserved for search parties still clinging
to hope, a hot potato they would have been

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:01.130
wise to abandon.

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:05.370
For while it was hope that brought these search
parties together, it was hope that sent them

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:07.960
off… never to be seen again.

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:13.810
The Foundation was then alerted to the occurrences
surrounding SCP-4608 by police reports accompanied

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:21.720
by a photograph…a photograph of an SCP-4608-1,
an organism consisting of unidentified plant-like

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:26.600
muscular structures and a periderm resembling
those found on common hardwoods.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:31.480
From the photograph alone, it was clear that
this 3-meter-tall organism was capable of

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:34.170
committing the violence recently endured.

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:39.330
Forceful in its demeanor, aggressive in its
presence, and territorial in its perception,

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:45.590
the photograph of SCP-4608-1 led to an even
bigger question… is this plant-like creature

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:49.020
grown by nature…or sown by man?

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:53.480
After extensive research by The Foundation,
records were retrieved that indicate the entirety

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:59.730
of the sixty-acre land was sown into life
by John Chapman in 1826.

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:03.870
Chapman was the type of man you could mistake
for a scarecrow, both for reasons of preferred

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:05.720
garb and body language.

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:07.710
He was treated as such too.

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:11.150
His personal space was respected…maybe too
much.

00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:15.870
He spent his life alone, only accompanied
and comforted by the things he planted.

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:22.060
He maintained these acres all by himself until
his eventual death in 1845, and it’s then

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:29.370
that it’s believed SCP-4608 became unstable,
reassigning its objective from comfort to

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:30.370
chaos.

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:35.330
When the newspaper came out the next Sunday,
John Chapman's obituary painted him as a priest

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:36.940
of the Allen county church.

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:39.220
But was this just the art of illusion?

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:44.990
For as far as we know, no records of a chapel
or congregation exist… a quiet choir indeed.

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:50.360
Come to think of it, it seems that everything
within this sixty-acre orchard was destined

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:56.650
to be silenced one way or another, by violent
force or even by conscious decision making.

00:06:56.650 --> 00:07:02.010
See, while the SCP has a long track record
of subduing anomalies by methods of capture

00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:06.350
and containment, not all things are suited
for locks and chains.

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:10.940
SCP 4608 is better covered with a story than
a tarp.

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:16.210
A fruitless field that once produced at an
unmanageable pace is now rendered incapable

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:17.669
of supporting growth.

00:07:17.669 --> 00:07:20.050
Most will think it’s due to a toxic spill.

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:25.880
In truth, the spill wasn’t that of chemicals
on soil… but rather corpses on crops.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:32.050
A week after receiving the photograph of 4608-1,
Site-81 sent a three-man investigation team

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:33.230
to Milan.

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:37.590
Their adventure was equally abrupt: a story
with no reportable beginning or middle but

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:39.870
simply a predictable end.

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:44.240
After four days of no communication, the Foundation
presumed the three agents no different than

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:46.480
their steak dinner, dead meat.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:51.270
And only then, after The Foundation’s failure
to solve the case, was it understood that

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:56.830
what we were to be looking for wasn’t people
at all…but rather answers to more nebulous

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:57.830
questions.

00:07:57.830 --> 00:07:59.690
What’s really happening here?

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:02.100
And why is this happening?

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:06.790
Following the loss of communication with the
investigation team, Site-81 dispatched a high-risk

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:12.040
response team, Mobile Strike Force Bravo-7,
aka Hometown Heroes.

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:16.120
These men had all the makings of heroes, and
they were determined to prove themselves worthy

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:17.130
of that title.

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:22.500
While Alpha squad moved north toward the incident
site, BETA squad headed east and GAMMA squad

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:27.620
hurried west – the crews covering all directions
of the compass but south, a coincidentally

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:31.770
symbolic gesture as if to say we will not
be taken down!

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:33.950
The mission was simple in theory.

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:36.589
Find out what happened to the previous team
and why.

00:08:36.589 --> 00:08:40.890
But, alas, missions never are as easy as their
objective statement reads.

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:44.870
In practice, some might even call them…impossible.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:48.660
As ALPHA headed near the incident site, they
noticed the shadows on the ground beneath

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:51.690
them did not resemble the shape of the leaves
in the canopy above.

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:55.850
They heard small drops of liquid tap tap tap
on their helmets.

00:08:55.850 --> 00:08:58.510
Yet, it wasn’t raining… was it?

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:03.200
ALPHA-1 ran his finger across the top of his
helmet and then examined the residue left

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:04.200
on his skin.

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:06.440
It was raining…just not water.

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:07.440
“Oh, god!”

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:11.710
Upon looking up, he witnessed the reasons
for both irregularities.

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:16.050
Bodies hung from branches by their intestines,
casting shadow puppets with their lifeless

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:17.050
limbs.

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:19.060
Blood dripped down like a leaky faucet.

00:09:19.060 --> 00:09:20.710
“What did this?”

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:25.041
But before he could even ponder the answer,
he heard a loud shriek from his radio, so

00:09:25.041 --> 00:09:29.610
loud that the radio itself vibrated, shaking
its way loose from his hand and falling to

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:30.610
the dirt.

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:35.220
He bent down and picked it up and this time
gripped tighter, as if to tell whoever is

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:38.410
responsible for that noise that they will
not get away that easily.

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:43.370
He and his crew followed the sound like a
game of Marco Polo, blind to what may be ahead.

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:47.650
They extended their guns and pointed them
into the distant tree line, like zombie arms

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:53.310
reaching outward in the pool toward the resonates
of “Polo”, a small comfort in a giant

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:54.770
game of distress.

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:59.440
As they pressed forward, ALPHA Squad proceeded
past all signs that pointed them back, stepping

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:02.140
over dead bodies like puddles on a rainy day.

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:06.170
Soon they found themselves crouching down
next to human remains, attending brief and

00:10:06.170 --> 00:10:11.560
hurried funerals for all their closest comrades,
torn between staying to pay respect and marching

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:12.940
along to earn it.

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:16.740
The chest cavities of the fallen had been
ripped open and filled with apples.

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:19.700
A grim foresight into what they were up against.

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:23.830
But nothing they could ever imagine would
prepare them for what they were about to see.

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:26.190
And they wouldn’t have to wait long.

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:27.940
Another loud shriek from ALPHA–1’s radio!

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:30.770
It shot free from his grip and again landed
in the dirt.

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:35.160
The squad tried to ignore the metaphorical
implications of this recurrence, quickly picking

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:39.500
up the radio and shrugging it off as if the
five-second rule applied equally to communication

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:41.470
systems as candy bars.

00:10:41.470 --> 00:10:45.680
They pressed forward, maybe out of bravery,
maybe out of shame of going back.

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:49.990
And while moving through trees, they began
to notice something alarming etched on their

00:10:49.990 --> 00:10:50.990
bark.

00:10:50.990 --> 00:10:51.990
What was it?

00:10:51.990 --> 00:10:55.090
There were unnaturally deep grooves on the
base of almost every one of the trees.

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:57.440
But what exactly were they from?

00:10:57.440 --> 00:10:59.500
Scratches from an animal or beast?

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:00.500
Infection?

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:01.500
Decay?

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:02.770
Their eyes drew closer.

00:11:02.770 --> 00:11:05.160
But proximity brought them no clarity.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:10.180
These sigils and symbols could be dated back
to occult Norse religion, but in that moment

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:15.390
they were incomprehensible to the men, yet
the message, even if misinterpreted, was very

00:11:15.390 --> 00:11:17.480
clear: beware!

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:18.860
Another shrieking cry over the radio.

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:20.320
“The bullets…the bullets aren’t…

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:21.640
they aren’t working.

00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:22.640
They can’t.

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:24.440
They can’t penetrate the bark!”

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:28.800
The grass is no greener over on the eastside
of the orchard, where BETA SQUAD gets lunged

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:31.680
at by an 4608-1.

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:36.590
Their defenses are futile, but they fight,
nonetheless, sending rounds to the attacker’s

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:38.120
chest - leading to…

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:39.120
Nothing.

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:44.730
If SCP – 4608 had a health meter, it wouldn’t
have budged in the slightest.

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:48.720
Understanding the negligible impact of their
efforts and assessing their injuries, BETA

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:53.180
SQUAD scurries to retreat to an abandoned
chapel, taking a brief refuge from war only

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:54.560
later to be named.

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.960
Quickly, they barricade the door.

00:11:56.960 --> 00:12:01.029
In the chapel, Beta-9 tends to BETA-6’s
wounds, who is in the worst shape of them

00:12:01.029 --> 00:12:03.540
all: cut, bloody, and beaten.

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:07.470
As he lays there grimacing, he shines his
flashlight up and down the chapel’s walls

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:10.540
until he finds a reason to stop and hold it
steady.

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:13.120
Illuminated is an assortment of human skulls.

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:17.930
And if this wasn’t traumatic enough, he
then spotted apple seeds embedded in BETA-6’s

00:12:17.930 --> 00:12:21.840
wounds - Apple seeds that were starting to
sprout.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.580
Beta-9 gave it to him straight.

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:25.110
“This is going to hurt.”

00:12:25.110 --> 00:12:28.630
He drew his knife from his belt and lowered
it into his comrades' wounds.

00:12:28.630 --> 00:12:32.920
Beta-9 dug into flesh and bone, picking the
seeds out, one by one.

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:36.160
Beta-6’s scream shook the chapel’s stained-glass
windows.

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:40.930
As BETA-1 stood guard, he saw a blur rip past
him, as if life had suddenly been turned up

00:12:40.930 --> 00:12:42.500
to three times speed.

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:44.910
He spun around in a circle to try to keep
his eyes on it.

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:48.270
But as his vision refocused, he saw BETA-9
was now dead.

00:12:48.270 --> 00:12:53.390
He then shifted his gaze to BETA-6, who was
looking less and less human by the second.

00:12:53.390 --> 00:12:57.260
Branches began sprouting out of his body like
an all-consuming magic beanstalk.

00:12:57.260 --> 00:12:58.410
Out of his chest.

00:12:58.410 --> 00:12:59.410
Out of his eyes.

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:00.410
Out of his mouth.

00:13:00.410 --> 00:13:05.270
And when there were no more orifices to exit,
his body exploded, making way for the new

00:13:05.270 --> 00:13:07.410
form that had overtaken him.

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:09.399
The barrage of branches broke through the
windows, and the squads fell like dominos.

00:13:09.399 --> 00:13:10.399
Dominos not just tapped over gently but kicked
by a toddler on full tilt.

00:13:10.399 --> 00:13:12.620
Only two were lucky enough to be on the outskirts
of inertia.

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:16.850
Outside, GAMMA-1 was on his knees thanking
his dead comrade for the grenade he stole

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:17.980
from his back pocket.

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:20.570
“I could always count on you to have my
back.

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:21.680
Even in death.”

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:27.399
One hand holding a grenade and the other on
his radio, Gamma-1 called off Alpha-7: “Alpha-7.

00:13:27.399 --> 00:13:28.950
Request for backup rescinded.

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:29.950
Go grab a burger.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:31.640
I’ll take it from here.”

00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:38.370
Gamma-1 slowly glanced up and locked eyes
with SCP-4608-2, a large apple tree with 13

00:13:38.370 --> 00:13:44.120
human faces embedded into it, a perennial
plant with great powers, a gymnosperm that

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:45.240
has found a voice.

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:49.570
Blood poured from SCP – 4608 – 2’s empty
eye sockets.

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:52.519
Gamma-One smirks: “Get some eye drops, sicko.”

00:13:52.519 --> 00:13:54.321
He crawled over to the beast.

00:13:54.321 --> 00:13:56.750
The faces begin yelling at him in indescribable
tongues.

00:13:56.750 --> 00:14:01.270
“Let me refer you to a speech therapist,”
he jokes as he pulls the pin of the grenade

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:04.320
and throws it toward the largest of the thirteen
mouths.

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:10.209
SCP – 4608-2 chokes on the grenade, forcing
it to inhale deeply… the strength of its

00:14:10.209 --> 00:14:13.000
lungs pulling Gamma – 1 toward it and sucking
him in.

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:14.970
The grenade goes off.

00:14:14.970 --> 00:14:17.030
SCP-4608-2 explodes.

00:14:17.030 --> 00:14:20.200
The surrounding trees scream and combust.

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:25.160
The orchard goes up in flames, the bodies
of the fallen are given an appropriate cremation.

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:27.470
Gamma–1’s radio lay face up on the dirt.

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:29.320
A voice rattles it awake.

00:14:29.320 --> 00:14:30.320
It’s Alpha–7.

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:31.320
“Gamma–1.

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:32.320
Gamma-1, you there?

00:14:32.320 --> 00:14:33.950
Can you hear me?

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:35.020
Please.

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:38.230
Please, Gamma -1?”

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:44.170
On October 16, 1947 ALPHA-7 was recovered
by the Allen County Fire Department, unconscious

00:14:44.170 --> 00:14:47.190
and suffering from exhaustion and smoke inhalation.

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:51.420
The Site-81 Concealment Team took control
of the situation and quarantined the area

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:53.709
using the cover story of a toxic chemical
hazard.

00:14:53.709 --> 00:14:54.709
Following debriefing and a psychological evaluation,
ALPHA-7 was administered amnestics and switched

00:14:54.709 --> 00:14:55.709
to low-risk recovery assignment.

00:14:55.709 --> 00:14:58.850
The members of MTF Bravo-7 were posthumously
awarded the Foundation Star for their efforts

00:14:58.850 --> 00:15:03.290
during the neutralization of SCP-4608.

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:06.350
And so, the one question that remains is…
how?

00:15:06.350 --> 00:15:13.870
How did SCP -4608-1 become so dangerous, and
how did its danger slip by for so many years?

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:17.130
Is its volatility by nature, design, or consequence?

00:15:17.130 --> 00:15:21.310
Could it be that the Foundation failed to
understand the complexity of this creation?

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:26.340
During Chapman’s lifetime, there were no
accidents or fatalities coming from SCP – 4608.

00:15:26.340 --> 00:15:33.209
Yet, there is no reason to believe that SCP
– 4608 -1 wasn’t always capable of harm.

00:15:33.209 --> 00:15:38.149
Maybe it always was capable of mass murders,
but simply had no reason to kill.

00:15:38.149 --> 00:15:41.390
What if the logging company never stepped
foot on that land?

00:15:41.390 --> 00:15:44.360
Never brought out their sharp blades and heavy
machinery?

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:48.100
What if this perilous orchard was in fact
docile, but provoked?

00:15:48.100 --> 00:15:52.510
What if the proverbial tree only falls in
the woods when we force our philosophy on

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:53.510
it.

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:59.060
Though SCP -4608-2 spoke in unidentifiable
sounds, the noises were always recognized

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:01.110
and recorded as language.

00:16:01.110 --> 00:16:04.260
It spoke with intent, even if misunderstood.

00:16:04.260 --> 00:16:05.959
What it screamed is still unclear.

00:16:05.959 --> 00:16:07.720
Were they pleas for help?

00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:09.360
Or messages of hate?

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:11.530
And would one even be worse than the other?

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:16.579
John Chapman might argue, when facing heavy
machinery and trained artillery, would raising

00:16:16.579 --> 00:16:20.000
your voice even be a moral decision at all?

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:24.130
Is fight or flight imbued not just in blood…
but also in bark?

00:16:24.130 --> 00:16:30.380
Now go check out “SCP-1472 - Multiverse
Strip Club” and “SCP-4840 - The Flying

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:34.329
City of Audapaupadopolis” for more thoroughly
cursed anomalous locations!

